k:Shaki|Shaki]] (cow tripe)\n* [[Cookbook:Stockfish|Stockfish]]\n* Nigerian [[Cookbook:Dryfish|dryfish]]\n* [[Cookbook:Bouillon Cube|Bouillon cubes]]\n* 3 cooking spoons [[Cookbook:Palm Oil|red palm oil]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Ogiri|ogiri]] Igbo\n* Assorted [[Cookbook:Meat and Poultry|meat]]\n* Assorted fresh [[Cookbook:Fish|fish]]\n* [[Cookbook:Ground Crayfish|Ground crayfish]]\n* Ground [[Cookbook:Chiles|chile pepper]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# [[Cookbook:Boiling|Boil]] the cocoyams until soft. Peel them, and use a [[Cookbook:Mortar and Pestle|mortar and pestle]] to pound them to a smooth paste.\n# Boil the shaki, stockfish, and dryfish in 1 liter of water for about 45 minutes over medium heat.\n# Add the beef and stock cubes and continue cooking until well done.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n* Tearing the ora leaves prevents the vegetables from becoming darker in color, as they would when sliced with a knife.\n\n[[Category:Nigerian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ashanti pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes for soup]]\n[[Category:Recipes using meat]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fish]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground crayfish]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dehydrated broth]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dryfish]]\n[[Category:Recipes using palm oil]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Ora Soup II","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"2-3","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"8 medium-sized corms cocoyam, washed","sourceText":"8 medium-sized corms cocoyam, washed","amountText":"8 medium-sized corms cocoyam, washed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 bunch ora leaves, torn into small pieces and rinsed","sourceText":"1 bunch ora leaves, torn into small pieces and rinsed","amountText":"1 bunch ora leaves, torn into small pieces and rinsed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"Uziza leaves, washed and minced","sourceText":"Uziza leaves, washed an